  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">CUPP · Research Release v1.2.1 — finder + full evidence trail</span>
            <h1>Choose the job first. Then choose the printer.</h1>
            <p>An evidence-first guide to consumer UV printers for makers and small businesses. Start with what you want to produce, see the best-fit configurations complete with a transparent scoring breakdown, then inspect the full engineering detail, every cited source, and a real cost-of-ownership estimate — not just a one-line verdict.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#finder">Find my printer →</a>
              <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#compare">Compare all configurations</a>
            </div>
            <div class="stats" aria-label="CUPP dataset summary">
              <div class="stat"><b>8</b><span>Printer families</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><b>16</b><span>Configurations</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><b>37</b><span>Sources logged</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><b>44</b><span>Evidence records</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><b>3</b><span>Shipping retail</span></div>
              <div class="stat"><b>Aug 2 '26</b><span>Last research pass</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="hero-card">
            <h2>What CUPP changes</h2>
            <p>This build merges the guided finder with the full CUPP evidence model: every ranking shows its own math, and every printer card links to its complete sourced detail.</p>
            <div class="signal"><span class="signal-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Best fit is contextual</strong><span>A tumbler shop and a raised-art studio should not receive the same ranking.</span></div></div>
            <div class="signal"><span class="signal-icon">5</span><div><strong>Evidence confidence stays visible</strong><span>Confidence reflects source quality—not how good the machine is.</span></div></div>
            <div class="signal"><span class="signal-icon">!</span><div><strong>Unknowns remain part of the answer</strong><span>Missing head prices, support terms, and long-term maintenance are never hidden.</span></div></div>
            <div class="signal"><span class="signal-icon">$</span><div><strong>Cost of ownership is computed, not guessed</strong><span>A real 1/3/5-year calculator, honest about which line items are disclosed vs. unknown.</span></div></div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="finder">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div><div class="kicker">Guided finder</div><h2>Build a shortlist in under a minute.</h2><p>Select the work you care about, set practical limits, and CUPP will rank configurations by fit while keeping buying risk visible.</p></div>
        </div>
        <FinderIsland client:load printers={printers} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence-band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker" style="color:#ffad84">Evidence, not hype</div><h2>Three separate questions drive every recommendation.</h2><p>A product can be promising yet unproven. Another can be well documented but a poor fit for your workflow. V4 keeps those distinctions explicit.</p></div></div>
        <div class="evidence-grid">
          <article class="evidence-card"><span class="score-dot">1</span><h3>Does it fit the job?</h3><p>Process, rotary support, object clearance, print area, ink configuration, and required accessories.</p></article>
          <article class="evidence-card"><span class="score-dot">2</span><h3>Can you buy it responsibly?</h3><p>Retail availability, preorder maturity, campaign fulfillment, service path, warranty, and consumables.</p></article>
          <article class="evidence-card"><span class="score-dot">3</span><h3>How strong is the evidence?</h3><p>Primary documentation, independent measurement, owner reports, unresolved conflicts, and missing data.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="benchmarks">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Measured reality</div><h2>Two real jobs beat a page of “up to” claims.</h2><p>These are measured eufyMake E1 examples from Tom’s Hardware. They are job examples, not cross-printer benchmarks.</p></div></div>
        <div class="benchmark">
          <div class="benchmark-intro"><h3>Raised work is a time-and-white-ink business.</h3><p>Relief height can dominate cycle time and consumable use. CUPP benchmarks should record layer strategy, white, gloss, cleaning waste, labor, failed attempts, firmware, and sponsorship—not only finished dimensions.</p><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://www.tomshardware.com/3d-printing/eufymake-e1-review" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the measured review →</a></div>
          <div class="job-grid">
            <article class="job-card"><h4>Textured phone case</h4><div class="duration">1 hr 12 min</div><div class="job-specs"><div class="job-spec"><span>Texture</span><b>0.4 mm</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>Total ink</span><b>4.5 mL</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>White</span><b>2.26 mL</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>Gloss</span><b>2.18 mL</b></div></div></article>
            <article class="job-card"><h4>12 × 16 textured canvas</h4><div class="duration">6 hr 55 min</div><div class="job-specs"><div class="job-spec"><span>Texture</span><b>2 mm</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>Total ink</span><b>46.27 mL</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>Ink cost</span><b>$19.89</b></div><div class="job-spec"><span>White + gloss</span><b>45.12 mL</b></div></div></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="compare">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Advanced comparison</div><h2>The complete engineering view, after you know what matters.</h2><p>The comparison currently tracks 16 consumer UV printer configurations from eight manufacturers, spanning a wide range of features, capabilities, and price points.</p></div></div>
        <p class="affiliate-disclosure"><strong>Affiliate disclosure:</strong> Some product links are affiliate links. Makersmiths Forge may earn a commission, at no additional cost to you. Affiliate compensation does not affect CUPP research, confidence ratings, or recommendations.</p>
        <CompareSection client:load printers={printers} />
      </div>
    </section>


    <section id="tco">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Cost of ownership</div><h2>What does it actually cost to run one of these for a year?</h2><p>Purchase price is one line in a much longer bill. This calculator uses only figures CUPP has actually sourced — a machine price, a disclosed ink rate, or a claimed maintenance figure — and clearly labels every line item that is genuinely unknown instead of quietly assuming a number.</p></div></div>
        <TcoSection client:load printers={printers} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="research">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Open research ledger</div><h2>The gaps are part of the product.</h2><p>CUPP does not convert missing information into a favorable score. These are the highest-value questions still needed for responsible buying recommendations.</p></div></div>
        <div class="research-grid">
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Replacement printheads</h3><p>Official part number, public price, calibration, downtime, replacement steps, and warranty impact.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Shipping-unit benchmarks</h3><p>Shared job files with time, ink or resin use, cleaning waste, photos, firmware, and failure notes.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Campaign fulfillment</h3><p>Verified delivery and current production timelines for LONGER, HeyGears, Morpho, Procolored, and iNew3D.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Soluble-support handling</h3><p>Removal time, temperature, residue, agitation, consumables, SDS, and wastewater guidance.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">05</div><h3>AI and software cost</h3><p>Active audit: credits, subscriptions, cloud dependency, offline use, export restrictions, OS support, licensing, and what stops when payment ends.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">06</div><h3>Long-term ownership</h3><p>Active audit: nozzle clogs, maintenance, warranties, support response, replacement parts, serviceability, firmware history, and ecosystem lock-in.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">07</div><h3>New-entrant watchlist</h3><p>Credible product-discovery signals get tracked here until there is a real announcement and specification sheet — never added to the comparison as a guess.</p></article>
          <article class="research-card"><div class="n">08</div><h3>Community-sourced cost figures</h3><p>Printhead replacement costs, ink consumption, and failure reports pulled from Facebook/Reddit communities need independent, non-anecdotal confirmation.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="watchlist-note"><strong>Anycubic — market watch, product unannounced (updated 2026-08-02):</strong> In July 2026, Anycubic invited users to participate in research on consumer-grade UV printers, with selected respondents considered for extended interviews. Anycubic also holds <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/CN115195127A/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chinese patent CN115195127</a>, covering multi-nozzle CMYK photosensitive-ink printing with UV-cured stacked layers for full-color 3D models. Together, these are credible signs of relevant research and product discovery, but Anycubic has not announced a commercial UV printer, specifications, pricing, or a release schedule. It remains outside the available-product comparison.</div>
        <div class="research-actions"><PrintheadInfoButton client:load /><p>Share owner tests and research leads with <strong>#CUPPUVResearch</strong>.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><strong><a href="https://www.makersmithsforge.com/">Makersmiths Forge</a> · CUPP — Consumer UV Printer Project</strong><br>Research Release v1.2.1 — updated 2026-08-02 from CUPP Master Workbook v0.9 and the latest owner, evaluator, campaign, and manufacturer evidence. Governed by the CUPP Project Constitution v1.0.<br><a href="https://www.makersmithsforge.com/about-us">About Us</a> · <a href="https://www.makersmithsforge.com/blog">Blog</a> · <a href="https://www.makersmithsforge.com/product-categories">Products</a> · <a href="https://www.makersmithsforge.com/faq">FAQ</a></div><div>Prices and campaign status change. Verify current terms before purchasing.<br>Some links are affiliate links; compensation does not affect CUPP research.<br>Cost-of-ownership figures are planning estimates, not purchasing guarantees.</div></div>
  </footer>

  <CompareBar client:load printers={printers} />

  <DetailModal client:load printers={printers} />

